  "problem": "${(\\frac{3}{7})}^{3}=$",
  "worked_solution": "To raise the fraction to the power of $3$, we must raise both the numerator and the denominator to the power of $3:$\n\n$$\n{(\\frac{3}{7})}^{3}=\\frac{{3}^{3}}{{7}^{3}}\n$$\n\nNow, using ${3}^{3}=27$ and ${7}^{3}=343,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{{3}^{3}}{{7}^{3}}=\\frac{27}{343}.\n$$",
